contents in all the milk samples ranged from (1.006–5.14 mg L−1). About 40% of milk samples showed variation
from the permissible range (5 mg L−1) of iron contents given by WHO. Minimum iron concentration (1.006 mg
L−1) of milk was observed when the buffalo were fed to maize silage for one month (Fig. 13).

