(Proshad et al., 2020). In contrast, the lowest Pb in vegetables (< 0.01 µg ­g−1) was found in the Mymensingh
and Chittagong districts, followed by the Jashore district
(0.19 µg ­g−1) (Supplementary Table S3). The lower Pb
content in vegetables in these districts might be related to
the light industrial activities in these areas as they are rural
or a less industrialized zone in Bangladesh (Alam et al.,
2003). However, in other districts, Pb content in vegetables was higher than 0.10 µg ­g−1 (Fig. 2). The increasing
order of Pb in vegetables (µg ­g−1) in different districts
